  - \( x_t \) depends on **lagged \( y \) (i.e., \( b_2 \neq 0 \))**,
  - **No spurious own-lag effects** (i.e., \( a_1, a_2, c_2, d_2 \) **insignificant**).

Thus, **\( b \) and \( d \) must be significant, while \( a \) and \( c \) must be insignificant** (to avoid own-lag dominance).

